\subsection*{Bareground cover}

While other cover classes seem to be stable bare ground appears to be disappearing from the Pember Fan (Figure \ref{fig:bare} \& \ref{fig:bgcover}).

A hurdle model was used to assess changes in bare ground cover (logistic regression to assess presence-absence followed by a beta binomial regression to determine proportion of bare ground)

The presence of bare ground was associated with  year (top ranked model: \emph{as.factor(Year) + (1 $\mid$ Plot/Subplot)}, AICc weight = 0.73) with bare ground diminishing over time (from an average of 18.2\%  in 2018 to 2.6\% in 2026).

Modelling suggest that the proportion of bare ground increased with proximity to the fence and was declining over time (top ranked mode: \emph{Year + scale(fence.dist) + (1 $\mid$ Plot/Subplot)}, AICc weight = 0.43). However this model had multimodal residuals, suggesting the possible hidden process. Graphing appeared to confirm that bare ground seems to appear in quantised clumps, suggesting that there may be underlying hidden process (Figure \ref{fig:multimodel}).

